            <ArticleTitle>Fistula formation from neovascularity developing in malignant fibrous histiocytoma of the heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1066-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neovascularity in cardiac tumours is uncommon and fistula formation from such neovascularity is extremely rare. Fistula formation from neovascularity developing in a malignant fibrous histiocytoma of the heart is described in a 48-year-old man. The the case illustrates that cardiac tumour is not only a cause of cardiac output obstruction but also of coronary artery fistula.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
